rsz: repair_timing -path_group takes a group the SDC defines

-path_group knew only reg2reg, in2reg, reg2out, in2out and gated_clock;
any other name warned (RSZ-0227) and repaired every path. A group made
with group_path, a path group through a set of nets for instance, could
not scope repair.

A name that is not one of the five but names a group the SDC defines is
taken as is: an endpoint is repaired when it has a path in that group,
and its group slack is the worst of those paths, as for the built-in
groups, without their structural endpoint classification.

The flattened Top (bazel-orfs tools/carve/top_level.tcl) repairs its
crossing group, the paths through the nets between two macros, so that
repair never works on a macro's own paths. 0208 keeps that group sound
when repair deletes one of its nets.

repair_timing_path_group7: a group -through one net is repaired, its
worst slack improving; a net named in a group_path -through is destroyed
through OpenDB, as a resizer move does, and write_sdc no longer names it. CRIT_VT_SWAP still
works on the fanin cone of the group's endpoints that some startpoint
reaches, as for the built-in groups.

Not upstreamed. Carried in bazel-orfs; retires on the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

